      "source_note": "Hand-curated from the opentelekomcloud-docs/regions-and-endpoints GitHub repository (raw.githubusercontent.com/opentelekomcloud-docs/regions-and-endpoints/master/doc/source/index.rst, retrieved 2026-08-11) and the T Cloud Public compliance pages (t-cloud-public.com/en/products-services/core-services/certifications; t-cloud-public.com/en/blog/benefits/bsi-c5-soc-2-typ-2; retrieved 2026-08-11). Rebrand note: Open Telekom Cloud was renamed T Cloud Public by Deutsche Telekom in 2026; provider ID stays 'otc' for SWAO stability; documentation remains at docs.otc.t-systems.com. Operator: T-Systems International GmbH, Deutsche Telekom subsidiary, German/EU entity, no US parent, KRITIS-registered; CLOUD Act does not attach via ownership or operations. Certifications BSI_C5/ISO_27001/SOC_2 confirmed for both regions per certification page. TISAX Level 3 confirmed for both regions. IT-Grundschutz: application submitted 2025-07-28, listed on BSI website 2025-09-19 under BSI-IGZ-0757; audit begins January 2026; certificate expected Q4 2026 -- NOT yet issued; populate certifications when published. KMS BYOK: documented in tracker issue #1385; direct documentation at docs.otc.t-systems.com/key-management-service was blocked by Anubis anti-bot (2026-08-11) -- UNVERIFIED; review before upgrading key_custody claim. Freshness caveat: the RST endpoint table is auto-propagated from T-Systems internal Gitea (last sync 2026-03-03); the table is approximately two years stale relative to the live portal; treat the service list as a lower bound. Helmut is clarifying the authoritative current source directly with T-Systems; update catalogue and bump confidence when confirmed (tracker #1385, OQ-3). Swiss T Cloud Public (T-Systems Switzerland, data centres Bern + Zollikofen, FINMA scope) is a separate product and operator -- NOT covered by this file; see design 095 OQ-1."
    },
